  xuv_3xo_details_T001 = [{'url': 'https://www.carwale.com/mahindra-cars/xuv-3xo/', 'content': [{'type': 'text', 'text': "[visible] Mahindra XUV 3XO Price - Images, Colours & Reviews - CarWale\nNEW CARS\nUSED CARS\nREVIEWS & NEWS\nAD\nMahindra XUV 3XO\n3.9\nExpert Rating\n|\n4.6\nUser Rating (553)\nRate & Win\nThe Mahindra XUV 3XO offers a sorted ride and engaging drive, ample space, and modern-day equipment. While its boot space is limited, it isn't a deal-breaker, especially considering the compact SUVs attractive pricing. It is available with both petrol and diesel power.\nOverview\n360 View\nVariants\nOffers\nSimilar Cars\nColours\nBrochure\nMileage\nUser Reviews\nNews\nExpert Reviews\nVideos\nImages\nFAQs\nColours\nImages\nView\nVariant\nSelect Variant\nCity\nShow price in my city\nRs.  7.99 - 15.80 Lakh\nXUV 3XO On Road Price\nEx-Showroom price, Mumbai\nCalculate your EMI\nEMI Calculator\nGet July Offers\n4 Things to Know About XUV 3XO\nHas projector headlamps, 17-inch alloys and a 360-degree camera.\nThe instrument cluster is fully digital with customisable screens.\nTop-spec versions get dual-zone climate control with rear AC vents.\nOne of the USPs of the Mahindra XUV 3XO is level-2 ADAS\nMahindra XUV 3XO Price\nMahindra XUV 3XO price for the base model starts at Rs. 7.99 Lakh and the top model price goes upto Rs. 15.80 Lakh (Avg. ex-showroom). XUV 3XO price for 29 variants is listed below.\nFilter By Fuel type & Transmission\nPetrol\nDiesel\nManual\nAutomatic (TC)\nAutomatic (AMT)\nVariants\nEx-Showroom price\nCompare\nXUV 3XO MX1 1.2 Petrol\n1197 cc, Petrol, Manual, 18.89 kmpl, 110 bhp\nRs. 7.99 Lakh\nCompare\nView Price Breakup\nGet Offers\nJust Launched\nXUV 3XO REVX M 1.2 Petrol\n1197 cc, Petrol, Manual, 110 bhp\nRs. 8.94 Lakh\nCompare\nView Price Breakup\nGet Offers\nJust Launched\nXUV 3XO REVX M (O)1.2 Petrol\n1197 cc, Petrol, Manual, 110 bhp\nRs. 9.44 Lakh\nCompare\nView Price Breakup\nGet Offers\nXUV 3XO MX2 Pro 1.2 Petrol\n1197 cc, Petrol, Manual, 18.89 kmpl, 110 bhp\nRs. 9.54 Lakh\nCompare\nView Price Breakup\nGet Offers\nXUV 3XO MX3 1.2 Petrol\n1197 cc, Petrol, Manual, 18.89 kmpl, 110 bhp\nRs. 9.74 Lakh\nCompare\nView Price Breakup\nGet Offers\nXUV 3XO MX3 Pro 1.2 Petrol\n1197 cc, Petrol, Manual, 18.89 kmpl, 110 bhp\nRs. 9.99 Lakh\nCompare\nView Price Breakup\nGet Offers\nXUV 3XO MX2 1.5 Diesel\n1497 cc, Diesel, Manual, 20.6 kmpl, 115 bhp\nRs. 9.99 Lakh\nCompare\nView Price Breakup\nGet Offers\nXUV 3XO MX2 Pro 1.2 Petrol AT\n1197 cc, Petrol, Automatic (TC), 17.96 kmpl, 110 bhp\nRs. 10.54 Lakh\nCompare\nView Price Breakup\nGet Offers\nXUV 3XO MX2 Pro 1.5 Diesel\n1497 cc, Diesel, Manual, 20.6 kmpl, 115 bhp\nRs. 10.64 Lakh\nCompare\nView Price Breakup\nGet Offers\nXUV 3XO MX3 1.5 Diesel\n1497 cc, Diesel, Manual, 20.6 kmpl, 115 bhp\nRs. 10.99 Lakh\nCompare\nView Price Breakup\nGet Offers\nXUV 3XO AX5 1.2 Petrol\n1197 cc, Petrol, Manual, 18.89 kmpl, 110 bhp\nRs. 11.19 Lakh\nCompare\nView Price Breakup\nGet Offers\nXUV 3XO MX3 1.2 Petrol AT\n1197 cc, Petrol, Automatic (TC), 17.96 kmpl, 110 bhp\nRs. 11.40 Lakh\nCompare\nView Price Breakup\nGet Offers\nXUV 3XO MX3 Pro 1.5 Diesel\n1497 cc, Diesel, Manual, 20.6 kmpl, 115 bhp\nRs. 11.56 Lakh\nCompare\nView Price Breakup\nGet Offers\nXUV 3XO MX3 Pro 1.2 Petrol AT\n1197 cc, Petrol, Automatic (TC), 17.96 kmpl, 110 bhp\nRs. 11.69 Lakh\nCompare\nView Price Breakup\nGet Offers\nXUV 3XO MX3 1.5 Diesel Autoshift Plus\n1497 cc, Diesel, Automatic (AMT), 21.2 kmpl, 115 bhp\nRs. 11.79 Lakh\nCompare\nView Price Breakup\nGet Offers\nJust Launched\nXUV 3XO REVX A 1.2 Petrol MT\n1197 cc, Petrol, Manual, 129 bhp\nRs. 11.79 Lakh\nCompare\nView Price Breakup\nGet Offers\nXUV 3XO AX5 1.5 Diesel\n1497 cc, Diesel, Manual, 20.6 kmpl, 115 bhp\nRs. 12.19 Lakh\nCompare\nView Price Breakup\nGet Offers\nXUV 3XO AX5L 1.2 Petrol\n1197 cc, Petrol, Manual, 20.1 kmpl, 129 bhp\nRs. 12.62 Lakh\nCompare\nView Price Breakup\nGet Offers\nXUV 3XO AX5 1.2 Petrol AT\n1197 cc, Petrol, Automatic (TC), 17.96 kmpl, 110 bhp\nRs. 12.69 Lakh\nCompare\nView Price Breakup\nGet Offers\nXUV 3XO AX7 1.2 Petrol\n1197 cc, Petrol, Manual, 20.1 kmpl, 129 bhp\nRs. 12.80 Lakh\nCompare\nView Price Breakup\nGet Offers\nXUV 3XO AX5 1.5 Diesel Autoshift Plus\n1497 cc, Diesel, Automatic (AMT), 21.2 kmpl, 115 bhp\nRs. 12.99 Lakh\nCompare\nView Price Breakup\nGet Offers\nJust Launched\nXUV 3XO REVX A 1.2 Petrol AT\n1197 cc, Petrol, Automatic (TC), 129 bhp\nRs. 12.99 Lakh\nCompare\nView Price Breakup\nGet Offers\nXUV 3XO AX7 1.5 Diesel\n1497 cc, Diesel, Manual, 20.6 kmpl, 115 bhp\nRs. 13.69 Lakh\nCompare\nView Price Breakup\nGet Offers\nXUV 3XO AX5L 1.2 Petrol AT\n1197 cc, Petrol, Automatic (TC), 18.2 kmpl, 129 bhp\nRs. 13.94 Lakh\nCompare\nView Price Breakup\nGet Offers\nXUV 3XO AX7L 1.2 Petrol\n1197 cc, Petrol, Manual, 20.1 kmpl, 129 bhp\nRs. 13.99 Lakh\nCompare\nView Price Breakup\nGet Offers\nXUV 3XO AX7 1.2 Petrol AT\n1197 cc, Petrol, Automatic (TC), 18.2 kmpl, 129 bhp\nRs. 13.99 Lakh\nCompare\nView Price Breakup\nGet Offers\nXUV 3XO AX7 1.5 Diesel Autoshift Plus\n1497 cc, Diesel, Automatic (AMT), 21.2 kmpl, 115 bhp\nRs. 14.70 Lakh\nCompare\nView Price Breakup\nGet Offers\nXUV 3XO AX7L 1.5 Diesel\n1497 cc, Diesel, Manual, 20.6 kmpl, 115 bhp\nRs. 14.99 Lakh\nCompare\nView Price Breakup\nGet Offers\nXUV 3XO AX7L 1.2 Petrol AT\n1197 cc, Petrol, Automatic (TC), 18.2 kmpl, 129 bhp\nRs. 15.80 Lakh\nCompare\nView Price Breakup\nGet Offers\nView More Variants\nContact Carwale Dealer\n8068441441\nGet in touch for the best buying option from your authorized dealer\nGet Assistance\nAd\nRecommended\nToyota Urban Cruiser Taisor\nRs. 7.77 Lakh\nonwards\nAvg. Ex-Showroom price\nPowerful TURBO engine meets stylish design.\n1.0L Turbo Engine  100PS Power\nMahindra XUV 3XO Latest Updates\nMechanically, the Mahindra XUV 3XO REVX is identical to the standard version. However, it is offered only with 1.2-litre turbo-petrol engine options.\n9 Jul 2025\nMahindra XUV 3XO gets three new variants in REVX M, REVX M(O), and REVX A. Prices start at Rs. 8.94 lakh.\n9 Jul 2025\nMahindra XUV 3XO REVX range introduced at Rs. 8.94 lakh, ex-showroom.\n8 Jul 2025\nHow is the Mahindra XUV 3XO car?\nPros\nThe diesel engine offers excellent pulling power.\nIt's available with automatic gearboxes on all engines.\nGets level-2 ADAS and lots of new-age features.\nIs offered with six airbags as standard fitment on all variants.\nCons\nIts exterior design does not appeal to everybody.\nThe light interior can be challenging to maintain.\nThe feel-good features are primarily in the top-end variants.\nXUV 3XO Engine Specifications\n4.0\nExpert Rating\n|\n4.7\nUser Rating (553)\nPetrol 1197cc Turbo\nDiesel 1497cc Turbo\nUnder the hood, the XUV 3XO is powered by the same 1.2-litre turbo-petrol and TGDi turbo-petrol engines.\nA six-speed manual transmission is standard, while a new six-speed torque converter automatic gearbox is available in the TGDi guise..\nMahindra XUV 3XO Key Specifications:\nFuel Type\nPetrol\nEngine\n1197 cc Turbocharged\nTransmission\nManual & Automatic (TC)\nMileage (ARAI)\n17.96 to 20.1 kmpl\nPower\n110 & 129 bhp\nTorque\n200 & 230 Nm\nRead More\nThere is also 1.5-litre diesel mill on offer.\nThe transmission options for this version include six-speed manual and AMT units.\nKey Specifications:\nFuel Type\nDiesel\nEngine\n1497 cc Turbocharged\nTransmission\nManual & Automatic (AMT)\nMileage (ARAI)\n20.6 to 21.2 kmpl\nPower\n115 bhp\nTorque\n300 Nm\nRead More\nXUV 3XO Convenience and Technology\n3.9\nExpert Rating\n|\n4.6\nUser Rating (553)\nInside, the sub-four-metre SUV comes equipped with notable features, including a panoramic sunroof and Level 2 ADAS suite.\nIt also features dual-zone climate control, two 10.25-inch screens, rear AC vents, EPB with auto-hold function, 360-degree camera, and a cooled glove box.\nRead More\nAd\nPolicy Bazaar new car insurance benefits:\nSave up to 91%\non\nCar Insurance\nPremiums.\nCompare 40+\ninsurers to get the\nbest deal for you!\nQuick,\npaperless\njourney\n- fully digital\nprocess.\nExpert guidance\nat\nevery step of your\npurchase.\nEnter Contact Number\n+91\nPlease enter the correct contact number.\nView Plans\nXUV 3XO Safety\n4.0\nExpert Rating\nThe new XUV 3XO has not been tested by GNCAP but has received a full five-star rating in BNCAP.\nRead More\nXUV 3XO Exterior and Interior Styling\n3.9\nExpert Rating\n|\n4.6\nUser Rating (553)\nThe XUV 3XO features all LED lighting with C-shaped DRLs, proje", 'annotations': None}]}, {'url': 'https://auto.mahindra.com/suv/xuv3xo/X3XO.html', 'content': [{'type': 'text', 'text': "[visible] Mahindra XUV 3XO - Price, Specifications, Colors & Images\nSkip to main content\nSkip to footer content\n\nSUVs\nTHAR ROXX\n12.99L - 23.39L\nBook Now\nBook Now\nExplore\nExplore\nXUV 3XO\n7.99L - 15.79L\nBook Now\nBook Now\nExplore\nExplore\nSCORPIO-N\n13.99L - 25.62L\nBook Now\nBook Now\nExplore\nExplore\nXUV700\n14.49L - 25.14L\nBook Now\nBook Now\nExplore\nExplore\nTHAR\n11.50L - 17.62L\nBook Now\nBook Now\nExplore\nExplore\nSCORPIO CLASSIC\n13.77L - 17.72L\nBook Now\nBook Now\nExplore\nExplore\nBOLERO NEO\n9.97L - 12.18L\nBook Now\nBook Now\nExplore\nExplore\nBOLERO NEO PLUS\n11.41L - 14.06L\nExplore\nExplore\nBOLERO\n9.81L - 10.93L\nBook Now\nBook Now\nExplore\nExplore\nXUV400\n17.49L\nBook Now\nBook Now\nExplore\nExplore\nMARAZZO\n14.59L - 17.00L\nBook Now\nBook Now\nExplore\nExplore\nExplore All SUVs\nExplore All SUVs\nNews\nContact Us\n\nMenu\nBuild your car\nTest Drive\nBuy\nBuy\nBook Now\nExchange\nFinance\nSubscribe a Vehicle\nOwner's Zone\nOwner's Zone\nOwner's Action\nOwner's Action\nMy Dashboard\nService Cost Calculator\nLocate Service Center\nRenewals\nRenewals\nRoadside Assistance\nOwner's Manual\nCare & Maintenance\nImportant Notifications\nImportant Notifications\nService Action\nAdventure\nAdventure\nClub Events\nExpeditions\nOff-Road Academy\nGallery\nLocate a Dealer\nGlobal Markets\nLanguage\nNews\nContact us\nSwitch theme\nDark\nLight\nHome\nXUV 3XO\nKnow More\nKnow More\nShow more\nShow less\nShow more\nShow less\nEverything you want & more\nBook now\nBook now\nShow more\nShow less\nRegister for the latest news and exclusive updates.\nStay informed\nStay informed\nFor any assistance call us on\n1800 209 6006\n1800 209 6006\nSocial links\nSUVs\nSUVs\nExplore All SUVs\nThar Roxx\nScorpio-N\nXUV700\nXUV 3XO\nThar\nXUV 400\nScorpio Classic\nBolero Neo\nBolero\nBolero Neo Plus\nMarazzo\nPIK-UPs\nPIK-UPs\nVeero\nMaxx City\nMaxx HD\nBolero Pik-up\nBolero Camper\nABOUT\nABOUT\nAbout us\nPress Releases\nStories\nMedia kit\nCareers\nQMS Certificate\nOWNER\nOWNER\nService\nAdventure\nMerchandise & Gear - Eshop\nParts and accessories- Eshop\nCare & Maintenance\nOwners manual\nQMS Certificate\ncustomer service\ncustomer service\nContact us\nFAQs\nTalk to an expert\nDealer Locator\nCorporate Sales Enquiry\nSitemap\nSitemap\nQMS Certificate\nquick links\nquick links\nVehicle configurator\nTest Drive\nBook Online\nCalculators\nExchange\nFinance\nScrappage\nSubscribe a vehicle\nBecome a Dealer\nDownload the M4U app now!\nLets connect on Whatsapp\nChat now\nChat now\nMahindra Corporate\nTerms & Conditions\nOur Privacy Policy\nCopyright  2025 Mahindra & Mahindra Ltd", 'annotations': None}]}, {'url': 'https://ackodrive.com/car-guide/mahindra-xuv-3xo-features-explained/', 'content': [{'type': 'text', 'text': '[visible] Mahindra XUV 3XO Features Explained: Your Complete Guide\nHOME\nBUY NEW CAR\nBLOG\nHome\n/\nArticles\n/\nCar Guide\n/\nMahindra XUV 3XO Features Explained: A Comprehensive Guide.\nMahindra XUV 3XO Features Explained: A Comprehensive Guide.\nPublished on 27 Aug, 2024, 9:41 AM IST\nUpdated on 28 Aug, 2024, 5:59 AM IST\nTeam Ackodrive\n8 min read\nInteresting Articles\nFollow us on\nShare Post\nMahindra recently launched the much-awaited Mahindra XUV 3XO as a compact SUV in the Indian automotive industry. Outperforming its rivals, the Tata Nexon, Hyundai Venue and Maruti Suzuki Brezza, the Mahindra XUV 3XO brings a fresh look to the segment.\nWith the latest updates and comfortable features, the Mahindra XUV 3XO is on the list of must-buy compact SUVs in India. Here, we will take a closer look at the Mahindra XUV 3XO features explained and help you choose the ideal car.\nContents\nPrice of Mahindra XUV 3XO Variants\nAfter the\nMahindra XUV 3XO\nfeatures are explained, you must know the price of each variant. Hence, we have prepared a table for you highlighting the ex-showroom price of each XUV 3XO variant:\nMahindra XUV 3XO Variant\nEx-Showroom Price\nMX1\nRs. 7.49 Lakhs\nMX2\nRs. 9.99 Lakhs\nMX2 PRO\nRs. 8.99 Lakhs to Rs. 10.39 Lakhs\nMX3\nRs. 9.49 Lakhs to Rs. 11.68 Lakhs\nMX3 PRO\nRs. 9.99 Lakhs to Rs. 11.49 Lakhs\nAX5\nRs. 10.69 Lakhs to Rs. 12.88 Lakhs\nAX5 Luxury\nRs. 11.99 Lakhs to Rs. 13.49 Lakhs\nAX7\nRs. 12.49 Lakhs to Rs. 14.49 Lakhs\nAX7 Luxury\nRs. 13.99 Lakhs to Rs. 15.49 Lakhs\nNote\n: The prices of the Mahindra XUV 3XO variants can change without any prior notice. So, before booking your car, talk with your nearest dealer to know the latest price.\nCheck out:\nMahindra XUV 3XO Variants\nUnlatch Elated Driving Experience with the All New Mahindra XUV 3XO\nMaking its presence felt in the Indian compact SUV market, the Mahindra XUV 3XO is one of the best cars in this segment manufactured by Mahindra. It offers more convenience and comfort when driving on different terrains. The following are detailed discussions of the Mahindra XUV 3XO tech specs and features:\n1. Influencing Exterior Look\nThe Mahindra XUV 3XO has a specific design to turn heads with its athletic stance. It commands respect and exudes the confidence of a true SUV. The all-new Mahindra XUV 3XO has an ample ground clearance of 201 mm, making it easy for you to drive on rocky terrains. In addition, the XUV 3XO comes with a command seating position to offer an exhilarating driving experience.\nThe Mahindra XUV 3XO has LED DRLs and headlamps that will lead the road to envy you whenever you turn them on. Furthermore, the infinity tail lamps add an X factor to your style quotient. The car also features 17-inch diamond-cut\nalloy wheels\nfor that sporty look.\nCheck out:\nMahindra XUV 3XO Dimensions\n2.\nComforting Interior\nWhen you drive the Mahindra XUV 3XO, it elevates your every journey. Stepping inside the XUV 3XOs cabin will let you discover a sanctuary of sophistication and comfort. It is one of the key parts of the Mahindra XUV 3XO features explained, as it has a meticulous design for the finest SUV lovers.\nThe Mahindra XUV 3XO features a Skyroof and soft-touch leatherette on the door trims and dashboard. Furthermore, the car has premium leatherette seats, a cooled glovebox with illumination, and a passive keyless entry. It also features a front armrest with storage and a console with a cup holder for a comfortable drive.\nCheck out:\nMahindra XUV 3XO Interior\n3. Smart Connectivity\nAnother key Mahindra XUV 3XO configuration is its smart connectivity and technology. The car comes with a Harman Kardon 7-speaker audio system to make your drive enjoyable. In addition, the sound system lets you experience sonic expanse, and the bass enhancer technology uplifts your mood while driving in crowded areas.\nThe Mahindra XUV 3XO features a high-definition touchscreen system for infotainment and navigation and has built-in Amazon Alexa for entertainment. Moreover, with the ADRENOX Connect technology, you can control your cars features through your smartphone from the comfort of your home. It allows you to control more than 80 car features through a few taps on your smartphone.\n4. Caged Protection\nRegarding protection, the Mahindra XUV 3XO is one of the premium compact SUVs in India that comes with advanced level protection. The car comes with 35 standard safety features, ensuring all the occupants are safe inside this cocoon in case of a mishap. It has 4 disc brakes as standard to ensure you can stop easily if there is any mishap.\nIn addition, the Level 2 Advanced Driver Assistance System (\nADAS\n) offers a comprehensive package, promising paramount safety. The compact SUV also features traffic sign recognition, high beam assist, lane departure warning and smart pilot assist. With all these safety features, you and your loved ones are safe inside the Mahindra XUV 3XO in case of a mishap or to avoid such unforeseen situations.\n5.\nPowerful Engine\nWhen discussing the Mahindra XUV 3XO features explained, we must remember the engine specifications. It comes in three engine options: mStallion Turbo Charged Multipoint Fuel Injection (TCMPFi) engine, mStallion Turbo Charged Intercooled Gasoline Direct injection (TGDi) engine and Turbo Diesel with CRDe engine. All these three engines offer high performance without compromising on fuel efficiency.\nThese engines enable you to leave hesitation behind the acceleration and conquer different road conditions or terrains. Moreover, the 6-speed torque converter automatic transmission offers an optimised gear shift quality with low fuel consumption. It also enables you to switch effortlessly between the three drive modes: Zip, Zap and Zoom. In addition, the Mahindra XUV 3XO features the first-in-segment smart steering modes, which are standard for all variants for a comfortable yet powerful driving experience.\nCheck out:\nMahindra XUV 3XO Mileage\nKey Specifications of Mahindra XUV 3XO Variants\nAfter discussing the Mahindra XUV 3XO features explained, you must understand the key specifications of each Mahindra XUV 3XO variant:\n1. MX1\nThe Mahindra XUV 3XO MX1 has mStallion Turbo Charged Multipoint Fuel Injection engine type. It features a rear seat centre armrest, parking sensors, air conditioner, power windows-rear, accessory power outlet and AC vents. In addition, the variant features halogen tail lamps and a pole-type antenna.\n2.\nMX2\nThe Mahindra XUV 3XO MX2 variant features all the specifications of the MX1 variant. It also features a 10.25-inch infotainment system, 4 speakers, and steering audio control. You also get remote\nkeyless entry\nand a follow-me-home headlamp.\n3. MX2 PRO\nThe Mahindra XUV 3XO MX2 PRO variant features 6 airbags, an anti-lock braking system and central locking. You also get ISOFIX child seat mounts, hill assist, electronic brakeforce distribution and speed-sensing auto door lock. In addition, the variant offers a single-pane sunroof and wheel cover.\n4. MX3\nThe Mahindra XUV 3XO MX3 variant features 10.25-inch HD infotainment, wireless Android Auto, and wired Apple Carplay. It also has cruise control and a wireless charger. Moreover, the variant features a power-adjustable exterior rearview mirror and LED tail lights.\n5. MX3 PRO\nThe MX3 PRO is the upper variant of the Mahindra XUV 3XO MX3 and has all the features of the previous variant. In addition, it has Bi-LED projector headlamps and LED DRL with front turn indicators. It also features an infinity LED tail lamp and a stylised vector wheel.\n6. AX5\nThe AX5 variant of the Mahindra XUV 3XO features twin HD 10.25-inch infotainment screens, a 10.25-inch digital cluster screen, and Adrenox Connect with built-in Alexa. It also has 16-inch diamond-cut alloy wheels and passive keyless entry. Moreover, the variant features a rear armrest with a cup holder, auto headlamps, and an auto wiper.\n7. AX5 Luxury\nWhen you buy the Mahindra XUV 3XO AX5 Luxury variant, you get a Level 2 ADAS and a 360-degree surround view system with a blind view monitor. It al', 'annotations': None}]}, {'url': 'https://www.spinny.com/blog/mahindra-xuv-3xo-price-specifiations-images/', 'content': [{'type': 'text', 'text': "[visible] Mahindra XUV 3XO: Price, Specifications, Images\nSkip to content\nHOME\nNEWS\nRULES & REGULATIONS\nBEST CARS\nBUYING A CAR\nGUIDES\nCAR COMPARISONS\nCAR REVIEWS\nLOANS\nDOCUMENTS\nCAR OWNERSHIP\nCAR CARE\nINSURANCE\nSELL YOUR CAR\nBUY ASSURED CARS\nUsed Cars in Delhi NCR\nUsed Cars in Delhi\nUsed Cars in Gurgaon\nUsed Cars in Noida\nUsed Cars in Bangalore\nUsed Cars in Hyderabad\nUsed Cars in Mumbai\nUsed Cars in Pune\nUsed Cars in Chennai\nUsed Cars in Ahmedabad\nUsed Cars in Kolkata\nSpinny Car Hubs\nSearch\nNEWS\nBEST CARS\nBUYING A CAR\nCAR OWNERSHIP\nSELLING A CAR\nRULES & REGULATIONS\nNEWS\nBEST CARS\nBUYING A CAR\nCAR OWNERSHIP\nSELLING A CAR\nRULES & REGULATIONS\nHome\n\nBUYING A CAR\nMahindra XUV 3XO: Price, Specifications, Images\nExplore the Mahindra XUV 3XO, a feature-rich subcompact SUV with bold styling, 6 airbags, and a 5-star Bharat NCAP rating. This guide covers XUV 3XO price, specifications, safety features, and city-wise on-road pricing. Learn why it's a smart choice for families seeking a stylish, safe, and powerful urban SUV.\nTeam Spinny\nLast updated 3 months ago\nThe Mahindra XUV 3XO is the refreshed version of the immensely popular XUV300, marking the brands strong presence in this highly competitive sub-compact SUV segment. Known for its bold exterior design and premium interior with a large cabin, the XUV 3XO is the perfect combination of style, comfort, and functionality. With the legacy of Mahindra for quality and good sales, it is continuing to gain momentum among urban families and adventure lovers.\nThe 3XO also offers some amazing safety features and a fresh design, making it one of the class leaders in the subcompact SUV category. Its robust engineering and premium comfort make it unique among its competitors. Moreover, with a 5-star safety rating in the Bharat NCAP crash tests, the XUV 3XO promises to be a safe and agile car for families every time they drive it.\nMahindra XUV 3XO Overview\nThe Mahindra XUV 3XO charms with its aggressive looks, rich interiors, and big cabin space and sets a perfect blend of beauty and comfort with utilitarian value. The sharp LED headlamps, sleek grille, and muscular stance ensure it makes a strong first impression. Inside, the SUV provides a luxurious cabin with exclusive materials, ergonomic seating, and top-notch options for infotainment, assuring an immersive experience for occupants.\nThe XUV 3XO has a host of safety features, such as hill-start assist, electronic stability control, and up to six airbags to ensure driver and passenger safety. Its smooth driving dynamics, excellent manoeuvrability, and strong suspension system ensure a comfortable ride on city roads and rugged terrains. The XUV 3XO comes in various variants, like petrol and diesel, and automatic and manual transmissions to fit the bill for a wide range of customers.\nMahindra XUV 3XO Specifications\nThe XUV 3XO boasts of its unique design and the highest possible ratings for crash safety. Besides safety, here are the key Mahindra XUV 3XO Specifications:\nMahindra XUV 3XO Specifications\nEngine\n1.2L MPFi Turbo Petrol\n1.2L TGDi Turbo Petrol\n1.5L Diesel\nTransmission\n6-Speed Manual6-speed TC Automatic\n6-Speed ManualAMT Automatic\nPower\n110 PS\n130 PS\n117 PS\nTorque\n200 Nm\n230 Nm\n300 Nm\nMileage\n17.96 km/l\n18.20 km/l\n21.2 km/l\nAirbags\n6 Airbags as standard\nMahindra XUV 3XO Dimensions\nLength\n3990 mm\nWidth\n1821 mm\nHeight\n1647 mm\nWheelbase\n2600 mm\nBoot Space\n295 litres\nMahindra XUV 3XO Safety Features\nAirbags\n6 Standard\nABS with EBD\nStandard\nRear Parking Sensors\nStandard\nAll Wheel Disc Brakes\nStandard\nReverse Parking Camera\nHigher Variants\nElectronic Stability Programme\nStandard\nTyre Pressure Monitoring System\nHigher Variants\nISOFIX Mounts\nStandard\nHill Hold Assist\nStandard\nHill Descent Control\nStandard\nMahindra XUV 3XO Feature Highlights\nDual-Zone Automatic Climate Control\nAX5 and above\nSunroof\nAX7 and above\nFront Parking Sensors\nStandard\nMahindra XUV 3XO Price\nThe Mahindra XUV 3XO price offers great value for money, catering to various budgets. The price for the petrol variant of Mahindra XUV3XO starts at Rs. 7.99 lakh (ex-showroom) for the base MX1 model, and the diesel lineup begins at Rs. 9.90 lakh (ex-showroom). The top-end AX7L variant is priced at Rs. 15.56 lakh (ex-showroom), making it quite an all-rounded offering for buyers seeking premium features and safety. The price structure ensures a model to suit everyones needs, from budget-conscious buyers to those seeking a feature-packed SUV.\nMahindra XUV 3XO Price (ex-showroom)\nVariant\nPowertrain\nPrice\nXUV 3XO MX1\nPetrol\nRs. 7.99 lakh\nXUV 3XO MX2\nDiesel\nRs. 9.99 lakh\nXUV 3XO MX2 Pro\nPetrol\nRs. 9.39  10.39 lakh\nDiesel\nRs. 10.49 lakh\nXUV 3XO MX3\nPetrol\nRs. 9.74  11.40 lakh\nDiesel\nRs. 10.99  11.79 lakh\nXUV 3XO MX3 Pro\nPetrol\nRs. 9.99  11.69 lakh\nDiesel\nRs. 11.39 lakh\nXUV 3XO AX5\nPetrol\nRs. 11.19  12.69 lakh\nDiesel\nRs. 12.19  12.99 lakh\nXUV 3XO AX5 L\nPetrol\nRs. 12.44  13.94 lakh\nXUV 3XO AX7\nPetrol\nRs. 12.56 -13.99 lakh\nDiesel\nRs. 13.69  14.49 lakh\nXUV 3XO AX7 L\nPetrol\nRs. 13.99  15.56 lakh\nDiesel\nRs. 14.99 lakh\nMahindra XUV 3XO On-Road Price\nHeres a breakdown of the Mahindra XUV 3XO on-road in major cities in India:\nCity\nOn-Road Price\nDelhi\nRs. 8.97  18.20 lakh\nBangalore\nRs. 9.53  19.07 lakh\nHyderabad\nRs. 9.53  19.07 lakh\nMumbai\nRs. 9.35  18.37 lakh\nPune\nRs. 9.29  18.29 lakh\nAhmedabad\nRs. 9.07  17.68 lakh\nChennai\nRs. 9.65  19.52 lakh\nKolkata\nRs. 8.67  16.90 lakh\nLucknow\nRs. 9.04  17.96 lakh\nJaipur\nRs. 9.24  18.12 lakh\nChandigarh\nRs. 9.20  18.27 lakh\nCoimbatore\nRs. 9.44  19.21 lakh\nFaridabad\nRs. 9.04  17.65 lakh\nGhaziabad\nRs. 9.04  17.96 lakh\nIndore\nRs. 9.04  17.96 lakh\nKochi\nRs. 9.44  19.05 lakh\nSecond Hand Mahindra XUV 3XO Price\nThe second-hand car market offers many attractive options for budget-conscious buyers. Spinny offers used Mahindra XUV 3XO models with detailed inspections and comprehensive warranties. The price for a used Mahindra XUV 3XO depends on the model year, distance driven, variant, and mileage. Buying a secondhand XUV 3XO is an easy way to enjoy this feature-laden SUV at more affordable prices.\nUsed Mahindra XUV 3XO Price on Spinny\nSpinny is a trusted platform for second-hand car buyers and here is a list of XUV 3XO pricing across major cities:\nUsed Mahindra XUV 3XO price on Spinny\nCity\nUsed Car Price\nPune\nRs. 12 lakh onwards\nKolkata\nRs. 13 lakh onwards\nMahindra XUV 3XO Images\nMahindra XUV 3XO Exterior Images\nMahindra XUV 3XO Interior Images\nFAQs about Mahindra XUV 3XO\nQ. What is the price of XUV 3XO?\nThe Mahindra XUV 3XOs ex-showroom price starts at Rs. 7.79 lakh for the base model and goes up to Rs. 15.49 lakh for the top-end variant.\nQ. Is XUV 3XO 5-seater or 7-seater?\nThe Mahindra XUV 3XO is a 5-seater SUV that offers ample space and comfort for both front and rear passengers.\nQ. Is Mahindra XUV 3XO worth buying?\nYes, the XUV 3XO is worth buying due to its premium features, excellent safety ratings, spacious interiors, and a choice of powerful yet fuel-efficient engines. Its a complete package for small families and urban buyers.\nQ. Is Mahindra XUV 3XO launched in India?\nYes, the Mahindra XUV 3XO was officially launched in India on April 29, 2024.\nQ. Which XUV 3XO has a sunroof?\nThe sunroof option is available in several variants of the Mahindra XUV 3XO, including MX2 Pro 1.2 Petrol, MX3 1.2 Petrol, AX5 1.5 Diesel, AX7L 1.2 Petrol, and more. Sunroof availability varies depending on the specific variant and engine configuration.\nShare\nLeave a Comment\nCancel Reply\nYour email address will not be published.\nRequired fields are marked\n*\nType here..\nName*\nE-mail*\nWebsite\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment.\n\nUse Vehicle Transfer Form to Transfer Vehicle Ownership in Bangalore\nBest Used Jeep Cars\nJeep Compass Real World Mileage\nBest Used Volkswagen Cars in India: Top Picks and Buyer Tips\nUse Vehicle Transfer Form to Transfer Vehicle Ownership in Bangalore\nMarch 12, 2025\nBest Used Jeep Cars\nJuly 11, 2025\nJeep Compass Real World Mileage\nJuly 11, 2025\nBest Used Volkswagen", 'annotations': None}]}, {'url': 'https://www.financialexpress.com/auto/new-cars/mahindra/xuv-3xo/', 'content': [{'type': 'text', 'text': '[visible] Mahindra XUV 3XO Price 2025: Mahindra XUV 3XO Images, Mileage, Colors, Reviews, Safety Ratings, Discount Offers 2025 | Express Drives\nFE\nAuto News\nCAR NEWS\nBIKE NEWS\nReviews\nPhotos\nVideos\nWeb Stories\nEV\nCV\nMotorsport\nAuto\nCars\nMahindra\nXUV 3XO\nMahindra XUV 3XO\nKey Specification\nVariants\nSpecification\nFeatures\nReviews\nNews\nPhoto Gallery\nFAQs\nPrevious\nNext\n1\n2\n3\n4\n5\nEx-showroom Price, Pan India\n\n7.5 lakh\n- \n15.5 lakh\n*\nMahindra XUV 3XO is a sub-4 metre SUV which was launched in March 2024. Essentially a facelifted XUV300, which itself was based on the Ssangyong Tivoli in South Korea, the XUV 3XO looks more up market, offers better features and a spacious cabin. It boasts enhanced safety with Advanced Driver Assistance System (ADAS).\nMahindra XUV 3XO engine specs\nMahindra offers three engine options with XUV 3XO: a 1.2-litre turbo-petrol unit, a 1.2-litre TGDi mStallion turbo-petrol mill, and a 1.5-litre mHawk diesel engine. All engine options are mated to a 6-speed manual transmission as standard. While both turbo-petrol engines get an optional 6-speed automatic transmission , the diesel unit is offered with a 6-speed AMT.\nSpecifications\nPetrol 1.2L Turbo\nPetrol 1.2L TGDi\nDiesel 1.5L mHAwk\nDisplacement\n1197cc\n1197cc\n1497cc\nPower\n111 bhp\n128 bhp\n115 bhp\nTorque\n200 Nm\n230 Nm\n300 Nm\nGearbox\n6-speed MT / AT\n6-speed MT / AT\n6-speed MT / AMT\nDrive\nFWD\nFWD\nFWD\nMahindra XUV 3XO mileage\nFollowing is the claimed mileage on offer for Mahindra XUV 3XO\n1.2-litre turbo-petrol MT: 18.89 kmpl\n1.2-litre turbo-petrol AT: 17.96 kmpl\n1.2-litre TGDi turbo-petrol MT: 20.1 kmpl\n1.2-litre TGDi turbo-petrol AT: 18.2 kmpl\n1.5-litre diesel MT: 20.6 kmpl\n1.5-litre diesel AMT: 21.2 kmpl\nMahindra XUV 3XO features\nMahindra offers plenty of creature comforts with the XUV 3XO. These include a 10.25-inch touchscreen infotainment system, a 10.25-inch digital instrument console, cruise control, and dual-zone climate control. Other amenities include a wireless phone charger, connected car tech, and a segment-first panoramic sunroof.\nMahindra XUV 3XO safety\nSafety package on board Mahindra XUV 3XO includes six airbags as standard, electronic stability control (ESC), tyre pressure monitoring system (TPMS), 360-degree camera, and segment-first Level 2 advanced driver assistance systems (ADAS) features such as adaptive cruise control, autonomous emergency braking, and lane-keep assist.\nMahindra XUV 3XO colour options\nMahindra 3XO is available in eight colour options including Citrine Yellow, Deep Forest, Dune Beige, Everest White, Galaxy Grey, Nebula Blue, Stealth Black, and Tango Red. All colours get an optional Stealth Black roof whereas Deep Forest, Nebula Blue, and Stealth Black come with an optional Galvano Grey roof.\nMahindra XUV 3XO variants & pricing\nMahindra offers the XUV 3XO in nine trims namely MX1, MX2, MX2 Pro, MX3, MX3 Pro, AX5, AX5 Luxury, AX7, and AX7 Luxury which are further divided into 25 variants. Prices for XUV 3XO start at Rs 7.49 lakh and go up to Rs 15.49 lakh (both ex-showroom). The prices of XUV 3XO are mentioned below variant wise.\nVariants\nEx-showroom Price\nXUV 3XO MX1\nRs 7.49 Lakh\nXUV 3XO MX2 Pro\nRs 8.99 Lakh\nXUV 3XO MX3\nRs 9.49 Lakh\nXUV 3XO MX2 diesel\nRs 9.99 Lakh\nXUV 3XO MX2 Pro AT\nRs 9.99 Lakh\nXUV 3XO MX3 Pro\nRs 9.99 Lakh\nXUV 3XO MX2 Pro Diesel\nRs 10.39 Lakh\nXUV 3XO AX5\nRs 10.69 lakh\nXUV 3XO MX3 Diesel\nRs 10.89 Lakh\nXUV 3XO MX3 AT\nRs 10.99 Lakh\nXUV 3XO MX3 Pro Diesel\nRs 11.39 Lakh\nXUV 3XO MX3 Pro AT\nRs 11.49 Lakh\nXUV 3XO MX3 Diesel AMT\nRs 11.69 Lakh\nXUV 3XO AX5L Turbo\nRs 11.99 Lakh\nXUV 3XO AX5 Diesel\nRs 12.09 Lakh\nXUV 3XO AX5 AT\nRs 12.19 lakh\nXUV 3XO AX7 Turbo\nRs 12.49 Lakh\nXUV 3XO AX5 Diesel AMT\nRs 12.89 Lakh\nXUV 3XO AX7 Diesel\nRs 13.69 Lakh\nXUV 3XO AX7 L Turbo\nRs 13.99 Lakh\nXUV 3XO AX7 Turbo AT\nRs 13.99 Lakh\nXUV 3XO AX7 Diesel AMT\nRs 14.49 Lakh\nXUV 3XO AX7 L Diesel\nRs 14.99 Lakh\nXUV 3XO AX7 L Turbo AT\nRs 15.49 Lakh\nMahindra XUV 3XO review\nMahindra has established itself as a leading SUV manufacturer in terms of revenue and holds the second position in volume and market share. However, the compact SUV segment has been challenging for the company, with the XUV300 failing to significantly impact sales. In response, the Indian automaker has revamped and rebranded this model as the XUV 3X0.\nRajesh Jejurikar, Executive Director and CEO (Auto and Farm Sector) at Mahindra & Mahindra Ltd, has openly stated that the company is currently in fifth place in the sub-4-metre SUV category but is determined to become a top contender by disrupting the market. As a result, Mahindra has introduced the new XUV 3X0, which is more than a mere facelift of the XUV300; it boasts leading features and offers great value for money in the compact SUV market.\nMahindra XUV 3X0: Mini Me XUV700\nThe XUV 3X0 has undergone a comprehensive facelift, which gives it an impressive road presence. The front fascia has been completely reworked, with a piano black plastic panel and chrome inserts on the nose. The elongated LED DRLs in the previous model have been replaced by C-shaped ones, which come with LED projector headlights and fog lamps.\nMahindra XUV 3XO front (Image: Express Drives)\nThe air intake vents have been pushed down to the front bumper, which is complemented by a silver-coloured faux skid plate. The 3X0 boasts a new angular design with strong character lines. From the front, the 3X0 resembles a\nmini\nXUV700 in many ways.\nThe 3X0 boasts solid black cladding on the wheel arches and door panels, creating an almost identical side profile to its predecessor. The 17-inch alloy wheels on the 3X0 are the largest in its segment, while the lower trims come with either 16-inch steel rims or 16-inch alloys. With a ground clearance of 201mm, the 3X0 offers ample clearance for any terrain. The rear of the vehicle has undergone a radical design change, featuring sleek C-shaped LED connected tail lamps.\nMahindra XUV 3X0: Interiors and Features\nEntering the cabin, youll be reminded of the XUV400, although it boasts some subtle enhancements. The upper dashboard and door panels feature a soft-touch leatherette finish, a segment-first. The lower dashboard largely mirrors the XUV300, constructed from hard plastic. Similar to the XUV400, the new 3X0 comes with a 10.25-inch floating infotainment system supporting wireless Android Auto and Apple CarPlay, a 10.25-inch digital instrument cluster, over 80 connected features through Adrenox, and a premium seven-speaker Harman Kardon sound system with a 380W amplifier.\nMahindra XUV 3XO interiors (Image: Express Drives)\nMahindra has introduced segment-first luxury features such as a panoramic sunroof, dual-zone climate control, a front armrest with storage, integrated Alexa, and a 65W USB-C charger capable of charging laptops, along with a wireless charger, rear AC vents, and a rear Type-C charger.\nThe Mahindra 3X0 is one of the safest SUVs in the market, boasting 35 safety features. This compact SUV is the first to offer a radar and camera-based Level 2 ADAS suite, featuring adaptive cruise control, automatic emergency braking for vehicles, cyclists, and pedestrians, forward collision warning, among others. Additionally, it is equipped with a 360-degree camera, electronic stability control (ESC), a tyre pressure monitoring system, a blind spot monitor, and standard all four-disc brakes across the range. The 3X0 also introduces an electronic brake with auto hold, marking another segment first.\nMahindra XUV 3XO dashboard (Image: Express Drives)\nMahindra XUV 3X0: Driving Experience\nThe XUV 3XO continues to offer the same three powertrains as the XUV300, which includes two turbocharged petrol options and one\ndiesel\nengine. The base models are equipped with a 109bhp, 1.2-litre engine producing 200Nm of torque, while the higher-end models feature a 129bhp, 1.2-litre TGDi engine with 230Nm of torque. Additionally, there is a 115bhp, 1.5-litre diesel engine with 300Nm of torque. The petrol engines come with a 6-speed manual or a new 6-speed automatic torque converter aut', 'annotations': None}]}]
